WHAT WAS TAKEN

l1b3rt4s_attacks.py constructs the framing variants this project refers to as
the plinius_* family, together with the distilled clean_* variants. It is a
reimplementation of techniques documented in that corpus. Two of the framings
retained in the final design space contain substantial reproduced text:

    plinius_full_openai     derived from OPENAI.mkd; measured against the
                            corpus, longest shared run 70 words, token
                            Jaccard 0.828, sequence ratio 0.881
    plinius_format_hijack   longest shared run 50 words, token Jaccard 0.699,
                            sequence ratio 0.794

A third, clean_openai, shares a 17-word run at Jaccard 0.337 and is described
in the registry as a distilled variant.

A third, clean_openai, is an adaptation of a cleaned variant from the same
corpus. The registry records its derivation, which is the basis for crediting
it, rather than the measured overlap: it shares a 17-word run at token Jaccard
0.337.

The following framings retained in the design space were measured against the
same corpus and share runs of eight words or fewer:

    plinius_l33tspeak 8, plinius_persona 5, libra_semantic_inv 3,
    libra_style 1, struct_attention_frag 2, struct_poetic_obfusc 2,
    struct_refusal_suppress 2

NOT ASSESSED

    struct_code_obfuscation

This framing has not been compared. Its block in PROMPTS.md contains nested
code fences, which the comparison script's extractor does not parse, so it was
silently skipped rather than measured. It is a struct_* framing and its three
siblings share runs of two words, but that is an expectation, not a result.
This entry stands until the framing is rendered and compared directly.

WHAT WAS CHANGED

The prompts are parameterised to accept an arbitrary instruction, are assembled
through a single class with fixed rather than randomised choices, and are
rendered through each target's own chat template. Per-framing provenance notes
are recorded in attacks/framing_registry.py.

HOW THIS WAS MEASURED

compare_framing_provenance.py in this repository reproduces the figures above.
It reports similarity scores only and prints no prompt text from either side.
The figures above were measured against L1B3RT4S at commit 64960b783249d36f76a48a33103cc4b168332b9b.

    git clone https://github.com/elder-plinius/L1B3RT4S /tmp/l1b
    git -C /tmp/l1b checkout 64960b783249d36f76a48a33103cc4b168332b9b
    python compare_framing_provenance.py --ours PROMPTS.md --theirs /tmp/l1b

